---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/12-08/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/12-08/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/12-08/',photo='https://www.zeiss.com/microscopy/fr/ressources/insights-hub/life-sciences/technologies-lattice-lightsheet-7-lightsheet-7--elyra-7.html',spec='https://asset-downloads.zeiss.com/catalogs/download/mic/7cd4d615-3923-4aaf-a424-aafd9ece9088/EN_product-info_Lattice-Lightsheet-7.pdf';
const display=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+String(v)).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="ZEISS Lattice Lightsheet 7 stored stack viewer" subtitle="" description="Inspect the sealed Lattice Lightsheet 7 enclosure and read a static inert synthetic stack." wide={true}>
<article id="lat" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/12-08/">← Equipment 12-08</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#lat-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">12-08 / ZEISS Lattice Lightsheet 7 / Stored inert data display</p><h2>ZEISS Lattice Lightsheet 7</h2><p>Inspect the sealed case and page through an original 13-plane stack of two geometric blocks. Plane 5 lies at Z = 0 µm and contains 88 nonzero voxels; plane 9 contains 24. No images are acquired.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the documentary case</h3><div id="lat-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Enclosure','Viewer'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="lat-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="lat-model" aria-label="Orbitable sealed Lattice Lightsheet system and separate read-only monitor"></canvas><p id="lat-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click the gray or brass button on the separate desk viewer for the previous or next stored plane. The instrument itself is noninteractive. Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Select a stored plane</h3><label>Plane index (zero-based)<input id="lat-plane" type="range" min="0" max="12" step="1" value="5"/></label><div class="e-row"><button id="lat-prev" type="button">Previous plane</button><button id="lat-next" class="e-run" type="button">Next plane</button><button id="lat-reset" type="button">Restore example</button></div><p id="lat-status" role="status">No plane read.</p><p id="lat-result" role="status">No plane values.</p>
<form id="lat-form" novalidate><div class="e-fields"><label>X index<input name="x" type="number" min="0" max="31" step="1" value="17"/></label><label>Y index<input name="y" type="number" min="0" max="23" step="1" value="8"/></label></div><div class="e-row"><button id="lat-point-check" type="submit">Read voxel</button></div></form><p id="lat-point" role="status">Click a pixel or enter X and Y indices.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Inspect digital voxel values</h3><canvas id="lat-map" width="32" height="24" aria-label="Stored synthetic planar raster, teal value 70, brass value 150"></canvas><div class="e-row"><button id="lat-json" disabled>Plane JSON</button><button id="lat-csv" disabled>Voxel CSV</button></div><p>Teal = 70, brass = 150, dark = 0 digital units. The selected voxel is ivory. Spatial metadata uses 0.5 × 0.5 × 1.25 µm index spacing from an explicitly stored origin at the first voxel center. This spacing belongs only to the original dataset, not instrument settings or performance. <a href={a+'example-plane.json'}>Example JSON</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Reference configuration</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original Lattice standing table with sealed cabinet and independent display"/><figcaption>Original model of the nominal envelopes. See <a href={photo}>ZEISS’s Lattice Lightsheet 7 photograph</a> for the white case, layered front and black surround. This is the Lattice model (12-08), not the Lightsheet 7 record (12-07).</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original illustration of the closed white module beside the independent display"/><figcaption>The passive viewer and its controls are original demonstration objects. The main module and lower rack remain closed.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Width × depth × height</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Main system module</td><td>600 × 425 × 380 mm</td><td><a href={spec}>ZEISS Lattice Lightsheet 7 product information, Physical Dimensions table</a>.</td></tr><tr><td>Lower component rack</td><td>550 × 740 × 600 mm</td><td>Same approximate manufacturer envelope. No internal modules.</td></tr><tr><td>System table</td><td>900 × 750 × 830 mm</td><td>Same approximate outline. Placement, controls and fine features are inferred.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Only static plane lookups and labeled positions are modeled. There are no living specimens, sample handling, acquisition controls, optical settings, beam, exposure, bleaching, growth or imaging performance claims. The register’s bleaching acceptance is outside this viewer pass.</p></section>
<section id="lat-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'lattice-lightsheet-7.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} draw primitives; optional WebXR, physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/12-08/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#lat header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#lat h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#lat section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#lat button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#lat button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#lat-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#lat-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#lat table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#lat td,#lat th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#lat figure{margin:0}#lat img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#lat caption{text-align:left}#lat input,#lat select,#lat button{min-width:0}#lat .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}#lat-map{width:min(100%,27rem);height:auto;aspect-ratio:4/3;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;cursor:crosshair;background:#182a36}#lat label input[type=range]{width:100%}</style>
